From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:41:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme set the menu rows' height, margins and icon size

On a 640x480 screen menu rows were as high as their text (22 px),
their icons a little over a letter high and their content 10 px from
the edges, so a full-screen menu crowded its rows at the top and
left a third of the screen empty. A list cut its last row in half
at its bottom edge.

menutext gains rowHeight (a row's least height; groups keep theirs),
rowPadding (the margin inside rows), iconSize (the rows' icons) and
fullRows: a list then scrolls by whole rows and leaves out a row it
cannot show whole. Without them lists are unchanged.
